\section{Tiers B and C: interim results}
\label{app:nonlinear}

The values quoted here and in \cref{sec:experiments} are computed from the per-seed files in \texttt{results/raw/vit\_runs/} at experiment-repo commit \texttt{ae59eab} by \texttt{notes/tierB\_numbers.py} (output, with every per-seed value, per-cell mean and standard deviation, paired difference and interval, in \texttt{notes/tierB\_numbers.txt}); \cref{fig:nonlinear,fig:realdata} are drawn from the same commit.
Committed so far: 46 of the 51 primary Tier~B runs (seeds 0--2 of all nine one-factor cells and of the scale-$0.5$ and $m=0.25$ strong-decay cells and the scale-$0.5$ zero-decay cell; two seeds of the other five decay cells) plus the fourth reference seed, and 7 of the 18 Tier~C runs (reference, 3 seeds; scale $0.5$ and $m=0.25$, seeds 0--1). The remaining runs are still in progress.
The nonlinear summaries carry no $\Phi_j$, $\hat R$ or fixed-point count, so no linear-theory rank is drawn: the comparison with P3--P5 is of the direction of each change only, and P7 is not tested (\cref{app:details}).

\emph{Trajectories.} In every committed run the rank falls to a few directions and rises again only after the early window. In the reference cell the numerical rank is 24--32 at initialization, 6--19 at step 250, 3--5 by step 1{,}000 and 70--107 at step 6{,}000 (4 seeds); with the slow target ($\tau=0.999$) the minimum is at step 50 or 100 and the late rank stays at 33--39.

\emph{Late rank per cell} (seeds 0--2, in order; paired change against the same seed of the reference, 98, 107, 90).
Predictor scale $0.5$: 112, 82, 95 ($+14$, $-25$, $+5$); scale 2: 69, 78, 28 ($-29$, $-29$, $-62$; 95\% interval of the mean $-87$ to $7$).
Depth 1: 116, 67, 79 ($+18$, $-40$, $-11$); depth 3: 130, 100, 98 ($+32$, $-7$, $+8$).
Mask ratio $0.25$: 82, 83, 114 ($-16$, $-24$, $+24$); $0.75$: 88, 73, 65 ($-10$, $-34$, $-25$; $-53$ to $7$).
EMA $\tau=0.9$: 89, 113, 93 ($-9$, $+6$, $+3$); $\tau=0.999$: 39, 35, 33 ($-59$, $-72$, $-57$; $-83$ to $-42$).
With $n=3$ only the slow-target interval excludes zero; we make no population-level claim for the others.

\emph{AdamW decay pairing (coefficients $0$ / $10^{-4}$ / $5\times10^{-4}$; small-dose sensitivity, not P7).}
Scale $0.5$: 112, 95, 93 / 112, 82, 95 / 111, 85, 92 (means 100.0, 96.3, 96.0).
Scale 2, seeds 0 and 2: 70, 28 / 69, 28 / 66, 28.
Mask ratio $0.25$: seeds 0, 2 at zero decay 84, 104; 82, 83, 114 / 81, 82, 101 at the reference and strong coefficients.
Mask ratio $0.75$, seeds 0, 1: 88, 74 / 88, 73 / 87, 73.
Strong minus zero is $-1$, $-10$, $-1$; $-4$, $0$; $-3$, $-3$; $-1$, $-1$ in the 9 complete seed pairs: never positive and at most 10 directions, against a seed-to-seed s.d.\ of 10--30 within these cells.
With an isolated multiplier of $0.9991$ over a run (\cref{app:details}), this is the response to a small decay; it does not locate a threshold, and it does not show that the ViT's rank is insensitive to a decay of the size that moves the Tier~A boundary.

\emph{Early statistic (P6).} The number of aligned directions with positive log-slope over steps 25--250 exceeds the late rank by $73.5\pm8.4$ in the reference (4 seeds), by 87 on average at scale $0.5$ and by 17--154 in the depth, mask and slow-target cells, but falls short of it at scale 2 ($-43$ on average) and $\tau=0.9$ ($-97$), where almost no direction grows during the window: it is 1--2 at $\tau=0.9$ (late rank 89--113) and 189--191 at $\tau=0.999$ (late rank 33--39), the opposite order to the late rank.
This failure is not a test of \cref{prop:survival} in the ViT: in the reference only 11--30 of the counted directions exceed the rank threshold at step 25 and 7--24 of them stay aligned through the window, and when a direction must be resolved at step 25 (at least $10^{-2}$ of the largest eigenvalue) and keep an overlap of at least $0.8$, the median count over the three Tier~C reference seeds is 2 (\texttt{results/derived/vit\_transfer\_diagnostics.csv}); this filter is a sensitivity check, not a calibrated prediction.
The window precedes the growth that sets the late rank.

\emph{Tier~C.} Late rank 131, 149, 126 in the reference (early statistic 184--188), 154, 147 at mask ratio $0.25$ and 149, 156 at scale $0.5$. Probe accuracy after training and at the same seed's initialization: reference 44.4, 44.2, 45.2\% against 41.4, 42.0, 41.1\% (paired gain $3.1\pm1.0$ points, 95\% interval 0.7--5.5); $m=0.25$ 44.1, 44.0\% and scale $0.5$ 46.2, 44.4\% against 41.4, 42.0\% (gains $2.3$ and $3.6$ points, 2 seeds each). No Tier~C run collapses, and the probe does not separate the configurations.

